      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T09:40:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Inet4Address and Inet6Address is a subclass of InetAddress.\nI don\u0027t think we have a single standard way to convert the v4 address to the v6 address.\nOne way is v4-mapped v6 address but another way is putting the v4 address to the first 4 bytes of the 16 bytes v6 address.\n\nSo If we want Struct to handle conversion from v4 address to v6 address, we need a new Struct Type to tell Struct about how to convert.\nAlso, it\u0027s not clear how to convert byteBuffer to Struct.\nIf we put the v4 address to the first 4 bytes of 16 bytes, we can not distinguish if this was a v4 address or v6 address.\nMaybe it\u0027s fine to assume the address was v4 address if last 12 bytes are zero but I\u0027m not sure.\n\nFor this CL, I feel it\u0027s simpler to do this on the caller side.",
      "parentUuid": "7042d81e_3720c64a",
      "revId": "42d37bad8d69e53e166384eb6573efc48bd55aca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
